    <!--
        THE INVESTOR RELATIONS LEAD. Net new as of 2026-08-10 - no existing Lead carries this
        type and the backfill deliberately does not create any.

        SECURITY-LOAD-BEARING, same as the sibling type: the Lead_IR_Investor sharing rule is
        the only thing granting the Investor_Relations group access once Lead OWD is Private.

        NO APEX PATH CREATES THIS TYPE. The inbound email pipeline, the Broker Portal and lead
        conversion all stamp Acquisition_Broker explicitly. IR leads are created by hand or by
        a future IR intake that does not yet exist.

        ⚠ FIX 2026-08-10 (code review, CRITICAL) - EVERY PICKLIST ON THE OBJECT IS ENUMERATED
        BELOW - Salutation, GeocodeAccuracy, LeadSource, Status, Industry, Rating,
        Asset_Type__c, Broker_Priority__c, Deal_Type__c, Disqualification_Reason__c,
        Parse_Confidence__c and Sale_Process__c - because a record type file that omits a
        picklist silently drops ALL of that picklist's values from that type. This is the same
        rule already enforced under NDA__c, Contract_Review__c, Disposition__c and LOI__c; the
        original brief that produced this file omitted it, which was a plan defect, not a
        deliberate narrowing. The full value set was pulled from a LIVE ORG DESCRIBE
        (`sf sobject describe, sobject=Lead`), never from this repo's field files, because
        `sf project retrieve` unions local and remote picklist values and a repo field file can
        list values the org no longer has. Both Lead record types (this one and
        Acquisition_Broker) carry the IDENTICAL, COMPLETE value set with the SAME single default
        (Status = New) - narrowing either record type's values is a separate, deliberate change
        for later, and this fix is deliberately behaviour-neutral for every existing Lead. This
        type carries no existing rows today, so "behaviour-neutral" here means it is created
        with the full value set available from day one, matching its sibling.
    -->
